 "headline": "DNp33 is one of a small family of 5 types surviving the nonselective FDR.",
 "limitations": [
  "One statistic (R = P2/(lam1^2*m_out)), one null family (within-mass-stratum type-label permutation), one annotation release, three non-independent substrates sharing a graph and most cells.",
  "BH controls the FDR over TYPE MEDIANS, not over cells; DNp33's median is a 2-POINT statistic (direction only, never a magnitude -- L213 limit 1) and every other type's inherits the same caveat scaled by its member count.",
  "The permutation holds log-out-mass stratum and type SIZE, not neurotransmitter, side, neuropil or hemilineage composition -- which is exactly why Q225-2 can only DESCRIBE a shared-annotation family.",
  "The resolution floor is 5.00e-05, so p-values are censored there and the BH ladder cannot separate types tied at the floor.",
  "Q225-2's modal-label-per-type reduction discards within-type annotation heterogeneity.",
  "ANATOMICAL leg only: no row mask, no settle, no seed (L164).",
  "A nonselective survivor count de-circularises the TYPE claim only. The per-cell claims of L206-L212 keep their selected status; Kriegeskorte's step (3), an independent specimen, is L212's v783 leg."
